## 10. AI and Biometric Integration Strategy

Do not make the entire application depend on an unverified AI model.

Create replaceable interfaces for:

1. Face feature extraction and matching.
2. Liveness or presentation-attack detection.
3. Additional biometric verification.
4. Risk evaluation.

For the first runnable milestone, use deterministic mock adapters and clearly labelled synthetic results.

Then evaluate a compatible face model and liveness component. Document the model version, license, dependencies, test conditions and known limitations.

If a model cannot run reliably on the target laptop, preserve the interface and use the mock adapter for the remaining workflow. Do not silently substitute simulated results for actual inference.

The risk engine must use explicit, documented rules initially. Do not call it a trained AI model unless a model has genuinely been trained or evaluated for that purpose.

