## 14. Evaluation Criteria

Evaluate the prototype against measurable criteria.

### Functional correctness

- Does the original workflow execute in the correct order?
- Are successful and failed transactions handled correctly?
- Is PostgreSQL persistence working?

### Security

- Are mandatory verification failures rejected?
- Is authorization bound to the correct transaction?
- Is replay prevention effective?
- Does concurrent redemption preserve daily-limit correctness?
- Are operator and branch permissions enforced?
- Are audit logs useful without exposing sensitive information?

### Performance

Measure API response time, throughput and error rate under documented conditions.

Report median and 95th-percentile latency, sample size, environment and test method.

Do not treat an in-process test result as production banking performance.

### Biometric evaluation

When real models are configured, evaluate false acceptance, false rejection and presentation-attack performance using an appropriate, authorized test dataset.

When mock adapters are used, report workflow correctness only. Do not claim biometric accuracy.

### Usability

Assess workflow clarity, error messages, accessibility and completion time with appropriate test participants.

### Real-world relevance

Compare SecureCross with existing cardless withdrawal methods and non-home-branch procedures. Document the specific gap being investigated and collect user or banking-professional feedback where possible.

Do not claim superiority until evidence supports the claim.

